url: "https://github.com/Hereon-InstituteMS/openPASO"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.20543501
abstract: >-
  openPASO is an open-source Model Context Protocol (MCP) server
  that connects general-purpose LLM coding agents to nine independently
  developed simulation codes (FEniCSx, deal.II, 4C Multiphysics,
  NGSolve, scikit-fem, Kratos Multiphysics, DUNE-fem, FEBio, and the
  experimental SPARTA DSMC backend). It exposes a
  small set of shared tools for solver discovery, simulation
  preparation, mesh generation, run execution, multi-solver coupling,
  in-place solver development, and visualisation. A curated pitfall
  knowledge base, 26 cross-backend collation topics, and a mandatory
  critic-sub-agent workflow are used to verify simulations before
  they run.
